+``mediacodec`` (Android)
+    Renders ``IMGFMT_MEDIACODEC`` frames directly to an ``android.view.Surface``
+    with per-frame presentation timestamps, and renders subtitles/OSD into a
+    second, transparent ``android.view.Surface``. Requires
+    ``--wid=(intptr_t)(*android.view.Surface)`` and, for OSD/subtitles,
+    ``--vo-mediacodec-osd-surface=(intptr_t)(*android.view.Surface)``.
+    Hardware sessions require ``--hwdec=mediacodec`` (not ``-copy``); software
+    frames are rejected, since copying them in would connect the Surface as a
+    CPU producer and prevent a GL VO from binding it later.
+
+    The embedder owns geometry: the video Surface must be sized to the
+    aspect-corrected video rectangle (decoded buffers are scaled to the whole
+    Surface), while the OSD Surface's bounds define its independent canvas and
+    must be stacked above the video. Since decoded buffers go straight to the
+    system compositor, the decoder's dataspace (HDR) is preserved and no GPU
+    pass runs, but video filters and screenshots are unavailable.
+
+    ``--vo-mediacodec-video-rect=<vw>,<vh>,<left>,<top>,<right>,<bottom>``
+    supplies the applied video rectangle relative to the full OSD view.
+    The six signed decimal integers are updated atomically at runtime.
+    Viewport dimensions must be positive and right/bottom are exclusive;
+    negative margins are supported for zoom. Empty (the default) means that
+    geometry is unavailable. Invalid updates retain the last valid geometry.
+
 ``mediacodec_embed`` (Android)
     Renders ``IMGFMT_MEDIACODEC`` frames directly to an ``android.view.Surface``.
